# danYAAP

**A Forked AOSP Custom ROM based on YAAP**

</div>

## 🛠️ Getting Started

### 1. Initialize local repository
```bash
repo init -u https://github.com/danYAAP-EXT/manifest -b seventeen --git-lfs
```

### 2. Sync up
```bash
repo sync -c -j$(nproc --all) --force-sync --no-clone-bundle --no-tags
```

---

## ⚙️ Build Flags

You can customize your build by defining the following flags in your device makefile (e.g., `device.mk` or `yaap_<device>.mk`):

### 📦 GApps Configuration
To include GMS (GApps) in your build:
```makefile
TARGET_BUILD_GAPPS := true
```

### 👤 Maintainer Information
To set the maintainer name shown in About Phone:
```makefile
# Example:
TARGET_MAINTAINER := "vlxlxlv"

# Usage (replace with your name):
TARGET_MAINTAINER := "<your_name>"
```

---

## 🏗️ Building

### 1. Set up the build environment
```bash
. build/envsetup.sh
```

### 2. Lunch a target
```bash
lunch yaap_<device_codename>-cp2a-userdebug
```

### 3. Start compiling
```bash
m yaap
```
